#!markdown

# Task

A task can be created by a dispatcher for any worker, or by a worker for himself only:

A task has mutable properties:
- Instructions
- Feedback
- A schedule (Not yet implemented)
  - Start date/time
  - Do we need a tentative End date/time ?  
  - Do we need the possibility to schedule multiple blocks/days at once ?

\
The dispatcher (or worker himself) can attach to the task:
- One Worker
- One Client

These are implemented with the entity-reference pattern, which cannot enforce a many-to-one relation, but suggests it.

\
The dispatcher (or worker himself) can attach to the task:
- Multiple Tools
- Multiple Yards  (Visit multiple yards of a single client to, for example, spray one after another with fertilizer ....)
- Multiple Consumables

These are implemented with the membership pattern, which suggests a many-to-many relationship.

YardName and YardAddress are no longer stored as successors of Task, as their historic value is irrelevant for a task.

